WEBVTT

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:09.130
<i>I will be useful to the captain, to the team!</i>

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:12.380
This story is a work of fiction. All persons and organizations are imagined. 
The kabaddi and game rules which appear in this anime are drawn from the original work.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:30.000
<b>Kouyou</b>

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:30.000
<b>Noukin</b>

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.620
Kouyou, three points gained!

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:04.620
<i>After Giving
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hEvery Last Drop</i>

00:02:01.130 --> 00:02:03.480
One minute left. A five-point gap.

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:05.270
And the captain is out...

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:07.270
<b>OUT: Misumi, Ban, Ojo</b>

00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:15.900
Now... it's time for defense.

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:19.240
<i>As Sakura is now, he has no openings.</i>

00:02:19.670 --> 00:02:22.620
<i>With the remaining time, 
we'll get at most two more raids.</i>

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:24.790
<i>If I count defense, we have three turns.</i>

00:02:25.270 --> 00:02:28.720
<i>Damn it. I can't bring myself 
to look the others in the eyes.</i>

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:30.970
<i>What am I doing?</i>

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:33.290
<i>Misumi...</i>

00:02:34.110 --> 00:02:37.380
<i>If I gave you some casual encouragement, 
would it help you get back on your feet?</i>

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:44.830
Number 6, Striker and Raider, heading out.

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:50.850
<b>Defense
Kouyou 7 Players</b>

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:50.850
<b>Raider
Noukin / Yoigoshi</b>

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:53.880
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:52.570
Let's take him down!

00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:53.860
Sir!

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:57.250
<i>Just kidding! We've got enough of 
a lead that we don't need to worry.</i>

00:02:57.250 --> 00:03:00.280
<i>We'll sacrifice one player 
and send Yoigoshi back!</i>

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:03.550
<i>What we need to do right 
now is use up the time!</i>

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:10.160
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:06.660
<i>If we do that, this match 
will end with Sakura's turn.</i>

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:09.180
<i>Stay wary and bring it on, Yoigoshi!</i>

00:03:11.210 --> 00:03:13.530
<i>He comes from a world where every 
point carries tremendous weight.</i>

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:18.730
<i>The fact that running the clock and 
killing time was a valid strategy</i>

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:20.630
<i>was something he'd learned 
through painful experiences.</i>

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:24.180
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:24.180
<i>You think I'll let you do that?!</i>

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:25.480
He rushed in!

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:26.970
It's a seven-man defense!

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:29.830
<i>Our current defense isn't
 set up for a takedown!</i>

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:32.190
<i>At this rate, we risk losing a lot of points!</i>

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:34.520
Forget the time! Send him back now!

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:36.360
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:43.530
<i>It isn't enough yet! Sakura's still in. 
I have to get more points!</i>

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:47.950
All right! Push him out!

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:55.880
Kabaddi!

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:56.880
Kabaddi.

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:58.130
Dodge!

00:03:58.130 --> 00:03:59.070
Kabaddi.

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:00.640
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:01.590
<i>His leg!</i>

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:02.810
<i>That's two...</i>

00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:05.900
<i>Not good! I'm off balance!</i>

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:06.720
<i>I can take him down!</i>

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:08.150
<i>This is bad! They'll come for a catch!</i>

00:04:08.150 --> 00:04:10.040
Kaba...ddi!

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:12.140
<i>Don't panic!</i>

00:04:12.410 --> 00:04:14.600
<i>Pick off more of them and make it back!</i>

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:17.690
Kabaddi...

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:18.280
<i>More...</i>

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:26.620
<b>Kouyou</b>

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:26.620
<b>Noukin</b>

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:25.570
Noukin, two points gained!

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:28.670
Okay! A three-point spread!

00:04:28.670 --> 00:04:30.680
You're amazing, Yoigoshi-kun!

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:38.800
You wanted another two points, didn't you?

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:40.240
Huh?

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:45.680
<b>BACK: Iura, Misumi</b>

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:45.680
<i>It seems like Yoigoshi and Hiro know.</i>

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:49.320
<i>For us to make a comeback, we needed 
to gain a lot of points there.</i>

00:04:49.790 --> 00:04:53.300
<i>Considering the time that's left, 
we only have one more chance to raid.</i>

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:58.410
<i>There won't be another chance 
for Masato to raid in this match.</i>

00:05:06.310 --> 00:05:07.350
<i>Yoigoshi?</i>

00:05:09.970 --> 00:05:11.860
<i>Yoigoshi did good work.</i>

00:05:12.890 --> 00:05:16.220
<i>It's just that he's up 
against the wrong opponent.</i>

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:23.630
Kabaddi. Kabaddi.

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:26.720
<i>This atmosphere is intense...</i>

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:30.090
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:30.720
<i>If we don't stop Sakura, 
the match is pretty much over!</i>

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:35.180
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:34.810
<i>There is no "next time."</i>

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:37.650
<i>I will end it here!</i>

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:38.190
Kabaddi...

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:38.930
<i>Stop him!</i>

00:05:38.930 --> 00:05:41.070
<i>The captain isn't here! 
I will protect Yoigoshi!</i>

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:42.040
Kabaddi!

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:44.810
Kabaddi!

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:48.060
<i>His moves are getting 
sharper and sharper!</i>

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:49.530
<i>What's with this guy?!</i>

00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:53.450
Azemichi!

00:05:55.900 --> 00:05:56.520
<i>Huh?</i>

00:05:57.710 --> 00:05:58.460
<i>Huh?</i>

00:05:58.460 --> 00:05:59.260
Kabaddi!

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:00.170
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:07.260
<i>Time's running out! I have to do the next raid!</i>

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:10.220
<i>Both of us at once... A five-point lead...</i>

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:12.360
<i>We'll lose!</i>

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:13.770
Kabaddi...

00:06:14.670 --> 00:06:17.720
<i>With even a single point gained, 
defeat is very likely.</i>

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:21.440
<i>A high-speed catch in the 
final stages of the game.</i>

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:24.720
<i>Willpower can cast aside fatigue.</i>

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:29.540
<i>However, it was the same for Sakura.</i>

00:06:32.790 --> 00:06:34.240
<i>I can't lose.</i>

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:35.740
<i>I won't lose!</i>

00:06:36.050 --> 00:06:38.200
<i>Through this match,
 I've realized how weak I am.</i>

00:06:38.690 --> 00:06:40.460
<i>I remembered what I must do!</i>

00:06:42.430 --> 00:06:44.030
<i>I am the ace.</i>

00:06:44.030 --> 00:06:47.170
<i>With my strength, I take 
my team... to the win!</i>

00:06:48.370 --> 00:06:49.380
Kabaddi.

00:06:49.730 --> 00:06:51.010
<i>There's an anti!</i>

00:06:52.510 --> 00:06:54.760
<i>His catch is weak. What is he aiming for?</i>

00:06:55.570 --> 00:06:57.270
<i>I don't have to take him down.</i>

00:06:58.230 --> 00:07:00.120
<i>Give your utmost best for the win.</i>

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:02.270
<i>Right, Yoigoshi?!</i>

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:05.900
Blocking?

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:07.730
<i>Number 3 was just buying time!</i>

00:07:08.090 --> 00:07:11.740
<i>I'm no match for him! Not alone!</i>

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:14.740
You're amazing, Kyo-chan!

00:07:15.320 --> 00:07:17.410
<i>Nothing scared me.</i>

00:07:17.980 --> 00:07:21.250
<i>I had guys with me, but even 
alone, I was unbeatable.</i>

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:25.240
<i>Man, they're really working hard.
 How is that fun?</i>

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:28.250
<i>I just don't get it.</i>

00:07:30.670 --> 00:07:32.930
<i>Alone... I can't stop him!</i>

00:07:36.910 --> 00:07:38.390
<i>Make it in time!</i>

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:40.890
<i>Taking him down is the only path left to us!</i>

00:07:43.180 --> 00:07:44.280
<i>I reached him!</i>

00:07:46.210 --> 00:07:47.400
Kabaddi...

00:07:48.090 --> 00:07:50.300
<i>I've learned during this match.</i>

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:52.270
<i>In a melee, what I need to be most wary of...</i>

00:07:52.270 --> 00:07:53.770
<i>is number 4's power.</i>

00:07:57.250 --> 00:07:59.410
<i>He's using the players 
coming for him as a shield!</i>

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:02.710
<i>I see! Without Date...</i>

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:04.110
<i>that spin will...!</i>

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:09.870
<i>This guy...</i>

00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:10.960
<i>He's not folding!</i>

00:08:11.270 --> 00:08:14.010
<i>Rough and unrefined, 
yet still he comes for me!</i>

00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:17.010
<i>I will stand and face him! I am not afraid!</i>

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:19.510
<i>I'll put everything I have into this spin...</i>

00:08:19.510 --> 00:08:21.380
<i>and shake off the likes of you!</i>

00:08:22.590 --> 00:08:23.980
Kabaddi!

00:08:28.170 --> 00:08:29.940
<i>He's not coming?</i>

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:36.140
You okay?

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:37.950
It isn't time for a break yet.

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:44.920
<i>People who've been doing this 
since forever are amazing.</i>

00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:48.990
You're amazing, Kyo-chan!

00:08:48.990 --> 00:08:50.460
How?

00:08:51.080 --> 00:08:54.720
Have you ever seriously 
devoted yourself to anything?

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:55.850
Nope.

00:08:56.470 --> 00:08:58.770
I've never done any sports.

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:02.910
<i>I have to do more... practice more, or else...</i>

00:09:04.670 --> 00:09:08.480
<i>If someone like me could 
predict Sakura's spin,</i>

00:09:09.390 --> 00:09:11.480
<i>it means I can take Sakura down.</i>

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:13.540
<i>And this situation is the result of...</i>

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:17.920
<i>Well, it wasn't just some fluke...</i>

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:20.880
<i>I can believe that, right?</i>

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:29.530
<i>I am...</i>

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:33.460
<i>Kouyou's...</i>

00:09:38.940 --> 00:09:42.080
<i>I know that, Ace!</i>

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:58.850
Kouyou, raid failed!

00:09:58.850 --> 00:10:00.840
Noukin, one point gained!

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:03.560
Y-You stopped him!

00:10:06.060 --> 00:10:08.550
Yeah!

00:10:08.550 --> 00:10:11.340
Did you see that, all you sportsmen?!

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:14.040
He offset the timing of his catch?

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:17.340
He sensed the danger and dealt 
with it in that instant.

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:20.680
Without experience and training, 
you could never pull off that defense.

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:24.250
Don't you ever look down on me!

00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:25.400
<i>Kyohei.</i>

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:28.600
<i>There's no need for you to intimidate 
everyone in the gym like that.</i>

00:10:29.640 --> 00:10:32.290
This is a new member, Misumi Kyohei-kun.

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:38.360
<i>You're already one of us.</i>

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:45.800
<i>You really went and did it, Senpai.</i>

00:10:47.710 --> 00:10:49.830
<i>This time, it's my turn.</i>

00:10:54.560 --> 00:10:55.180
Let's go!

00:10:55.180 --> 00:10:56.560
Kouyou, time out!

00:10:57.020 --> 00:10:59.430
Fifteen seconds remaining
and a two-point gap!

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:02.650
He sent Sakura-san out!

00:11:06.430 --> 00:11:09.030
At this critical moment...

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:11.790
Blast it. Blast!

00:11:11.790 --> 00:11:13.520
You did more than enough.

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:16.400
You did it.

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:20.030
The moment you sent Masato-san out, 
you'd already done your job.

00:11:20.970 --> 00:11:25.030
Get it, Ace? Leave the rest to us.

00:11:28.430 --> 00:11:30.000
It's our turn now.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.230
Do you remember what 
everyone around us said

00:11:32.230 --> 00:11:34.750
when we made it to Kanto's top eight?

00:11:35.410 --> 00:11:37.880
S-Sakura carried us as a one-man team.

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:40.790
And what I thought then... 
was that they were completely correct!

00:11:40.790 --> 00:11:42.120
Hey...

00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:43.650
What's wrong with that?

00:11:43.650 --> 00:11:47.680
Every day, we pit ourselves 
against that monster.

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:51.220
When Sakura's on the court, 
we prioritize protecting him.

00:11:51.220 --> 00:11:53.940
But the next defense will be different.

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:57.010
We've had a ton of practice 
against a monster.

00:11:57.010 --> 00:11:59.630
We can show them what our 
defense is truly made of.

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:02.910
We will win, as Kouyou.

00:12:04.030 --> 00:12:04.900
Sir!

00:12:08.190 --> 00:12:10.510
Honestly, you've all played so well.

00:12:10.510 --> 00:12:12.330
While I wasn't able to be there...

00:12:12.740 --> 00:12:14.550
What are you talking about?

00:12:14.550 --> 00:12:17.090
We could only do this because you're here.

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:19.800
For you to say that redeems me.

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:25.800
<b>Noukin</b>

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:25.800
<b>Kouyou</b>

00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:23.280
<i>But a comeback still seems difficult.</i>

00:12:23.820 --> 00:12:25.800
<i>We'd need to score three points...</i>

00:12:27.400 --> 00:12:28.870
<i>Every time this happens...</i>

00:12:29.280 --> 00:12:31.810
<i>I find myself at a loss as to what to say.</i>

00:12:32.430 --> 00:12:34.310
<i>The raider holds the key to a win or a loss.</i>

00:12:34.760 --> 00:12:36.950
<i>The rest of us can only watch.</i>

00:12:36.950 --> 00:12:38.500
If it were the captain,

00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:40.620
would he be able to make a 
comeback on the next raid?

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:42.280
Yoigoshi—

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:43.900
I'm not losing my nerve here.

00:12:44.470 --> 00:12:45.420
It's the opposite.

00:12:46.290 --> 00:12:49.540
You're the one who said it, right? 
"The Beast of Noukin."

00:12:49.540 --> 00:12:51.550
"Go become the strongest raider."

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:55.280
I've never once thought that was a joke.

00:12:57.410 --> 00:12:58.920
I'll tell you the plan.

00:13:00.080 --> 00:13:01.440
End of timeout!

00:13:01.440 --> 00:13:02.920
Raid goes to Noukin!

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:04.930
<b>Kouyou</b>

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:04.930
<b>Noukin</b>

00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:10.430
Noukin's final raid... is starting.

00:13:12.680 --> 00:13:15.440
<i>Normally, a little over ten 
seconds is nothing of note,</i>

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:18.190
<i>but here it transforms into unending time.</i>

00:13:21.070 --> 00:13:23.530
<i>In this incredibly volatile world...</i>

00:13:24.880 --> 00:13:26.530
<i>a beast has stepped forward.</i>

00:13:28.400 --> 00:13:29.990
They're going in to push him out!

00:13:30.550 --> 00:13:31.900
<i>A single point is allowable.</i>

00:13:31.900 --> 00:13:33.810
<i>I'll make a play that helps us win!</i>

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:37.000
<i>This guy... isn't running?</i>

00:13:37.710 --> 00:13:40.340
<i>For Yoigoshi, the battle began...</i>

00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:42.730
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:13:42.730 --> 00:13:44.510
<i>in this moment!</i>

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:49.520
<i>The zones running along the side 
of the court known as lobbies,</i>

00:13:49.520 --> 00:13:51.850
<i>become playable areas after 
the raider enters a struggle.</i>

00:13:52.510 --> 00:13:56.200
<i>In this moment, a meter on 
either side of the court,</i>

00:13:56.200 --> 00:13:58.540
<i>two meters in total, have been unlocked.</i>

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:00.250
Kabaddi!

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:02.490
<i>Now, I'll be able to use distance!</i>

00:14:03.700 --> 00:14:04.950
<i>The targets are far away...</i>

00:14:04.950 --> 00:14:06.570
<i>The defense has spread out.</i>

00:14:07.130 --> 00:14:08.880
<i>But I expected them to do this.</i>

00:14:08.880 --> 00:14:10.570
<i>I've crushed their teamwork!</i>

00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:15.520
There's no helping a lack 
of experience at this point.

00:14:15.520 --> 00:14:17.040
If that's the case, hone yourselves now!

00:14:17.720 --> 00:14:21.020
<i>As novices, though we may feel isolated, 
we'll devote everything we've got...</i>

00:14:21.020 --> 00:14:23.350
<i>We'll each dodge with everything we have!</i>

00:14:23.350 --> 00:14:26.090
<i>We'll each go to take him 
down with everything we have!</i>

00:14:26.570 --> 00:14:29.050
And, one day, those things 
will become Kouyou's...

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:32.600
our team's, strength!

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:34.310
He's been blocked in!

00:14:35.490 --> 00:14:37.060
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:14:39.580 --> 00:14:41.510
<i>A Back?! Why now?</i>

00:14:42.070 --> 00:14:43.080
Kabaddi!

00:14:44.550 --> 00:14:45.940
I'll tell you the plan.

00:14:47.100 --> 00:14:49.390
In order to prevent a huge point gain,

00:14:49.390 --> 00:14:51.210
it's likely they'll spread out their defense.

00:14:51.800 --> 00:14:53.270
And when you go in for a catch,

00:14:53.270 --> 00:14:56.800
they'll block the course for a 
Back or a Cut. That's certain.

00:14:57.330 --> 00:15:00.130
So, you should use their positioning,

00:15:00.130 --> 00:15:02.420
and create a trajectory targeting 
the remaining opponents.

00:15:02.950 --> 00:15:07.770
Using a skill you haven't mastered
 in a match carries high risks, but...

00:15:07.770 --> 00:15:10.050
It's like a penalty shoot-out.

00:15:10.500 --> 00:15:12.120
No matter what the outcome may be,

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:15.060
you never imagine yourself 
missing in a crucial moment.

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:19.060
<i>Ever since I was a kid, 
I've always... always...</i>

00:15:22.350 --> 00:15:23.810
<i>done things this way!</i>

00:15:25.070 --> 00:15:26.060
Kabaddi!

00:15:27.090 --> 00:15:28.550
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:15:30.010 --> 00:15:31.200
That's three!

00:15:31.560 --> 00:15:33.660
<i>He really clinched it!</i>

00:15:34.140 --> 00:15:35.310
Kabaddi...

00:15:35.310 --> 00:15:36.370
Now!

00:15:36.860 --> 00:15:38.970
<i>We will win with our strength!</i>

00:15:39.370 --> 00:15:42.370
<i>We won't lose! If we lose now...</i>

00:15:42.730 --> 00:15:45.210
<i>...then we won't be able to look Sakura,</i>

00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:47.970
<i>the guy who did all that for us, in the eye!</i>

00:15:49.900 --> 00:15:51.380
<i>He turned!</i>

00:16:00.750 --> 00:16:02.850
<i>There was always a genius beside me.</i>

00:16:03.330 --> 00:16:07.000
<i>I kept working hard so that 
I wouldn't get left behind!</i>

00:16:07.870 --> 00:16:12.360
<i>Brains, brawn... 
After giving every last drop...</i>

00:16:13.850 --> 00:16:16.700
<i>that's where you'll find 
the greatest of plays!</i>

00:16:18.020 --> 00:16:20.360
Go, Hiro!

00:16:26.390 --> 00:16:27.730
<i>A spin?!</i>

00:16:29.410 --> 00:16:30.620
<i>That's Sakura's—</i>

00:16:33.100 --> 00:16:35.900
<i>That's right... it isn't just me!</i>

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:38.720
<i>Every single one of these guys...</i>

00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:40.670
<i>Everyone is burning themselves to ash!</i>

00:16:51.650 --> 00:16:55.160
Don't you underestimate me!

00:16:59.970 --> 00:17:01.660
<i>Just one more step.</i>

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:03.660
<i>Always. Always!</i>

00:17:06.430 --> 00:17:08.750
<i>I will overcome this "one more step"!</i>

00:17:10.630 --> 00:17:13.290
<i>Overcoming everything...</i>

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:16.930
<i>is what I've decided to do!</i>

00:17:43.070 --> 00:17:45.120
Four points by touch! Two points by lona!

00:17:45.510 --> 00:17:46.840
End of match!

00:17:52.030 --> 00:17:56.180
All right!

00:18:00.650 --> 00:18:04.030
Yeah! Did you see that? That was my—

00:18:13.290 --> 00:18:14.980
What's with that face you're making?

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:16.650
I'm happy, but...

00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:19.020
there's a part of my heart...

00:18:19.020 --> 00:18:21.490
that's saying "he really got me," 
and I hate that part of me.

00:18:22.520 --> 00:18:25.190
That's how raiders should be.

00:18:25.190 --> 00:18:28.210
Besides, it's the end that 
decides a battle, right?

00:18:30.290 --> 00:18:31.800
I'm counting on you for the tournament.

00:18:32.330 --> 00:18:33.020
Yeah.

00:18:38.560 --> 00:18:40.400
<i>If only I'd stopped him...</i>

00:18:41.330 --> 00:18:42.360
Sakura...

00:18:42.940 --> 00:18:44.010
The thing is,

00:18:44.480 --> 00:18:46.470
back when I joined the team,

00:18:46.470 --> 00:18:50.150
more than winning, I thought this team
 seemed like it would be fun to join.

00:18:51.540 --> 00:18:52.960
But now, it's different.

00:18:54.250 --> 00:18:56.170
I want to win with this team.

00:18:57.060 --> 00:18:58.440
Please, lend me your strength.

00:19:01.500 --> 00:19:03.120
We'll get our revenge at the tournament!

00:19:03.690 --> 00:19:04.700
Yeah!

00:19:15.200 --> 00:19:17.620
"I wasn't able to do anything." Is that it?

00:19:19.470 --> 00:19:21.930
Starting now, I'll drill everything into you.

00:19:22.580 --> 00:19:27.310
Leave the judgment as to whether or not you could do anything for after that.

00:19:27.310 --> 00:19:28.430
Yes, sir!

00:19:29.020 --> 00:19:31.480
Ojo-san! Thank you very much.

00:19:31.920 --> 00:19:33.720
We should be the ones thanking you!

00:19:33.720 --> 00:19:36.160
That's one win, one loss, right, Sakura-kun?

00:19:36.160 --> 00:19:36.730
What?

00:19:36.970 --> 00:19:38.750
Our match.

00:19:38.750 --> 00:19:41.740
Thanks to you, I was able
 to realize a lot of things.

00:19:42.610 --> 00:19:44.090
The form might be a little different,

00:19:44.090 --> 00:19:46.360
but make sure you keep our promise, okay?

00:19:47.510 --> 00:19:49.250
<i>Our promise...</i>

00:19:49.710 --> 00:19:53.400
I will become a raider that can 
be a strength for you, Ojo-san...

00:19:54.810 --> 00:19:57.090
Will it really count as keeping the promise?

00:19:57.090 --> 00:19:59.210
It will totally count!

00:19:59.950 --> 00:20:02.220
<i>I'm really no match for 
him when he's like this...</i>

00:20:03.450 --> 00:20:05.330
Let's settle this at the tournament.

00:20:05.770 --> 00:20:06.460
Yeah.

00:20:07.690 --> 00:20:11.180
And I'll have to keep my 
promise to Yoigoshi-kun, too.

00:20:11.180 --> 00:20:12.080
Huh?

00:20:12.080 --> 00:20:15.210
I said that if I lost, I'd have 
to tell you why I quit kabaddi...

00:20:15.700 --> 00:20:18.340
Oh... It's fine.

00:20:18.340 --> 00:20:22.080
If it made someone as strong as you quit,
 it had to be something big, right?

00:20:23.470 --> 00:20:24.380
Thank you.

00:20:25.300 --> 00:20:27.850
Hey, Yoigoshi! How's the injury?

00:20:27.850 --> 00:20:29.330
Hey. It's fine.

00:20:29.330 --> 00:20:32.730
This is the second time in my life a 
junior player's taken a lona from me.

00:20:32.730 --> 00:20:34.140
You're truly incredible.

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:35.470
Who was it?

00:20:35.470 --> 00:20:36.330
Huh?

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:40.410
Who was the first junior to 
take a lona from you?

00:20:43.200 --> 00:20:47.720
If you both win your way through the 
tournament, you'll end up facing him.

00:20:48.590 --> 00:20:49.930
He's from the world team.

00:20:50.540 --> 00:20:52.120
The world team?

00:20:52.830 --> 00:20:54.170
I see.

00:21:01.230 --> 00:21:03.240
<b>Akagakubo Station</b>

00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:06.740
That Sakura shook my hand 
with freakin' crazy strength.

00:21:07.050 --> 00:21:09.580
That's an apprentice of 
the captain's for you.

00:21:09.580 --> 00:21:12.650
That's great, isn't it? He considers you a rival.

00:21:12.650 --> 00:21:14.750
He's the ace of a Kanto top-eight team!

00:21:15.290 --> 00:21:17.400
There's still people better than him, right?

00:21:17.400 --> 00:21:20.300
There goes Yoigoshi, 
saying stuff like that again.

00:21:20.640 --> 00:21:23.480
It's our first win! And you're 
the one who clinched it!

00:21:23.480 --> 00:21:25.460
Be happier! Show us how you feel!

00:21:25.460 --> 00:21:26.830
We need a toast! A toast!

00:21:26.830 --> 00:21:28.180
It was just a practice match.

00:21:28.430 --> 00:21:29.440
Why are they so excited?

00:21:30.490 --> 00:21:31.730
Hey, Yoigoshi...

00:21:32.800 --> 00:21:35.020
Kabaddi is fun, isn't it?

00:21:37.530 --> 00:21:39.370
If I can't win, it's boring!

00:21:41.730 --> 00:21:44.220
That's a dirty move, you know...

00:21:44.780 --> 00:21:47.040
Which means, in short...

00:21:47.040 --> 00:21:48.930
What did you mean by that?

00:21:49.930 --> 00:21:50.700
Oh, look. The train's here.

00:21:51.520 --> 00:21:52.540
What's going on?

00:22:19.230 --> 00:22:24.070
<b>Aim for
Number 1 in Japan!</b>
